{"type": "root", "attrs": {"index": "no"}, "body": [{"level": 0, "type": "title", "indent": 0, "text": ["Compositing"], "extent": [12, 28]}, {"type": "summary", "indent": 0, "text": ["Houdini\u2019s compositing networks let you create and manipulate images such as renders."], "extent": [28, 121]}, {"type": "warning_group", "body": [{"ext": null, "type": "warning", "indent": 0, "text": ["Old network"], "role": "item", "extent": [16, 38], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["As of Houdini 20.5, use ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/nodes/cop/index", "type": "link", "text": ["Copernicus nodes"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop/index.html"}, " instead of Compositing nodes. Though both networks still exist, the Compositing network is now designated as ", {"type": "code", "text": ["COP Network - Old"]}, ". The Compositing network and its nodes will be deprecated and then removed in a future Houdini release."], "extent": [38, 335]}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Overview"], "extent": [164, 179], "body": [{"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": ["If you are working with the Cineon file format, remember to set the\n  options on the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Cineon"]}, " tab of the global compositing preferences."], "extent": [179, 322]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": ["Create nodes to ", {"scheme": null, "value": "load", "type": "link", "text": ["load image data"], "fullpath": "/composite/load.html"}, " into the compositor."], "extent": [322, 385]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": ["Create nodes to ", {"scheme": null, "value": "layers", "type": "link", "text": ["blend or modify the image data"], "fullpath": "/composite/layers.html"}, "."], "extent": [385, 445]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": ["Set the ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/nodes/cop2/", "type": "link", "text": ["render flag"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/index.html"}, " of the node you want to provide the\n  final output of your compositing network."], "extent": [445, 563]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": [{"scheme": null, "value": "save", "type": "link", "text": ["Save the composited data as image files"], "fullpath": "/composite/save.html"}, ", or\n  ", {"scheme": null, "value": "export", "type": "link", "text": ["use the composited data elsewhere in Houdini"], "fullpath": "/composite/export.html"}, "."], "extent": [563, 674]}], "container": true}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["How to configure the compositor"], "extent": [674, 712], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["There are two kinds of compositing options in Houdini: ", {"type": "em", "text": ["global"]}, "\npreferences and defaults which affect all compositing you do in Houdini,\nand ", {"type": "em", "text": ["project"]}, " settings which affect a particular ", {"type": "code", "text": [".hip"]}, " file."], "extent": [712, 913]}, {"level": 3, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Global preferences"], "extent": [913, 940], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Choose ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Edit \u25b8 Preferences \u25b8 Compositing"]}, " to open the \n    ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/ref/windows/mainprefs", "type": "link", "text": ["compositing preferences"], "fullpath": "/ref/windows/mainprefs.html"}, "."], "extent": [940, 1057]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The preferences let you control memory usage, efficiency, interface,\n    and color behavior in the compositor."], "extent": [1057, 1173]}]}, {"level": 3, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Project settings"], "extent": [1173, 1198], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Choose ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Edit \u25b8 Compositing  Settings"]}, " to open the\n    ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/ref/windows/composite", "type": "link", "text": ["Composite Project Settings window"], "fullpath": "/ref/windows/composite.html"}, "."], "extent": [1198, 1320]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The settings in this window control the defaults for various COP\n    options in this scene file. Changing a project setting can affect\n    existing nodes that use that setting."], "extent": [1320, 1502]}]}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Types of compositing operators"], "extent": [1502, 1539], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["Most COPs belong to one of six groups. Each group has common parameters\nand a consistent way of behaving."], "extent": [1539, 1647]}, {"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["Generators"], "extent": [1647, 1659], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Create new images and generally create new planes."], "extent": [1659, 1715]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Generators create new planes. They all have the same parameters for\n    specifying the image and sequence information. Generators define the\n    following information:"], "extent": [1715, 1892]}, {"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Image information"], "extent": [1892, 1921]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Sequence information"], "extent": [1921, 1953]}], "container": true}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["If a generator has an input, it can either add a plane to the sequence\n    (", {"type": "q", "text": ["inline generation"]}, ") or affect an existing plane using a simple\n    operation (", {"type": "q", "text": ["quick composite"]}, ")."], "extent": [1953, 2137]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Planes are generated ", {"type": "q", "text": ["inline"]}, " when a generator adds a plane to an\n    existing sequence. A generated plane can have its own data type and\n    composition, it is not restricted to the input types."], "extent": [2137, 2342]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["A generator performing a ", {"type": "q", "text": ["quick composite"]}, " generates the plane and uses\n    a simple operation to combine the input plane (I) with the generated\n    plane (G). The simple operations are Add, Subtract, Multiply, Minimum\n    (Min), Maximum (Max), and Average. This is useful for creating masks or\n    slates, or adding noise to images."], "extent": [2342, 2685]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["These techniques have the following advantages:"], "extent": [2685, 2742]}, {"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["The frame range, resolution, interlace options and extend conditions\n      are inherited from the input. This makes matching the resolution and\n      frame range of another sequence much easier; if these are changed in\n      the input, they automatically update."], "extent": [2742, 3016]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["The number of nodes needed is reduced; no merge or composite node is\n      needed. This also boosts performance and memory efficiency."], "extent": [3016, 3162]}], "container": true}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Inline Generation or Quick Composite mode overrides most of the\n    operator\u2019s Image and Sequence parameters. Use the ", {"type": "q", "text": ["Add Plane"]}, " parameter\n    on the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Image"]}, " tab to specify the plane to create or modify, and the\n    operations to perform. If the plane specified does not exist, or the\n    operation is set to Rename or Replace, the generator creates a new\n    plane."], "extent": [3162, 3541]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["Scoped filters"], "extent": [3541, 3557], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Filter operations which may be applied to only specified planes,\n    channels or frames. Certain operations cannot be scoped, such as a\n    Scale or Crop COP (which changes the resolution)."], "extent": [3557, 3756]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["This family of operators allows an operation to be applied to selected\n    planes and frames. By default, all planes and frames are selected."], "extent": [3756, 3907]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Planes and channels that are not scoped are passed through as if the\n    node was bypassed."], "extent": [3907, 4008]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["You specify scoping with a space-separated list of planes. You can\n    specify specific channels with a dot followed by the channel name. YOu\n    can also use wildcards. For example:"], "extent": [4008, 4200]}, {"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["C A"]}, " "], "extent": [4200, 4212], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["Color and Alpha are scoped."], "extent": [4212, 4248]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["*"]}, " "], "extent": [4248, 4258], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["All Planes are scoped."], "extent": [4258, 4289]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["C.r"]}, " "], "extent": [4289, 4301], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["The red channel of color is scoped."], "extent": [4301, 4345]}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Scoped filters also have options for scoping frames:"], "extent": [4345, 4407]}, {"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": ["All"], "extent": [4407, 4416], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["All frames are scoped."], "extent": [4416, 4456]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": ["Inside Range"], "extent": [4456, 4474], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["All the frames within the frame range specified are scoped, with\n        optional drop-off regions at each end of the range."], "extent": [4474, 4616]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": ["Outside Range"], "extent": [4616, 4635], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["All the frames outside the frame range specified are scoped, with\n        optional drop-off regions at each end of the range."], "extent": [4635, 4778]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": ["Even/Odd Frames"], "extent": [4778, 4799], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["Only the even or odd frames are scoped."], "extent": [4799, 4856]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": ["Custom"], "extent": [4856, 4868], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["All of the frames in the custom list are scoped."], "extent": [4868, 4930]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["Masked filters"], "extent": [4930, 4946], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Affect portions of an image through the use of a mask. This mask is\n    another image which is similar to an alpha matte. Masked filters are\n    a type of scoped filter."], "extent": [4946, 5125]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Many operators let you apply them per-pixel using a ", {"type": "em", "text": ["mask"]}, " image. The\n    mask can be any plane or channel within the input sequence, or any plane\n    or channel in the sequence of the mask input."], "extent": [5125, 5331]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The mask acts as a stencil - wherever the mask is 1 (white), the\n    operation is performed. Wherever the mask is 0, the input pixel is not\n    affected. In between, the input pixel is linearly blended with the\n    output pixel. The mask can be inverted so that all pixels outside the\n    mask are affected instead."], "extent": [5331, 5656]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Use the Alpha plane as a mask as a very efficient way of masking color\n    correction operations to the actual image without affecting outside\n    black levels."], "extent": [5656, 5826]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["Pixel filters"], "extent": [5826, 5841], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Highly optimized operations that can be combined into a single\n    operation if they are grouped together in a chain. Pixel filters are\n    a type of masked filter."], "extent": [5841, 6015]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Houdini ", {"type": "q", "text": ["collapses"]}, " multiple consecutive pixel filters in a network\n    chain into a single cooking operation."], "extent": [6015, 6135]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Pixel filter node tiles have a ", {"type": "em", "text": ["light blue background"]}, " to distinguish\n    them from other types of nodes."], "extent": [6135, 6250]}, {"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Reduces quantization and cutoff errors by doing quantization once, at\n      the end of the pixel filter chain, rather than at every node."], "extent": [6250, 6399]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Uses less memory. Only 1 image is cooked, rather than making a copy\n      for each pixel filter."], "extent": [6399, 6507]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Calculates in floating point, preventing clipping and quantization\n      error of fixed formats (8- and 16-bit integer). Can handle pixel\n      values well above white and below black during the pixel chain without\n      being clamped, even if the image\u2019s native data format would clamp it.\n      The values are clamped at the end of the chain."], "extent": [6507, 6863]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["Reduces network and quantization overhead, resulting in faster\n      cooking."], "extent": [6863, 6952]}], "container": true}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["If you use a mask, it must be the same for all pixel filters in that\n    chain. Pixel filters with different masks will not collapse together.\n    Houdini will log a warning to notify you that quantization is occurring\n    at that node (to get rid of this warning, set the Quantize parameter to\n    ", {"type": "q", "text": ["At This Node"]}, ")."], "extent": [6952, 7277]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["If a pixel filter chain branches into two pixel filter outputs, each\n    output pixel filter will cook the chain independently of the other."], "extent": [7277, 7427]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["At any point in the chain, you can tell a pixel filter node to quantize\n    using the Quantize parameter. This will terminate the chain at that\n    point and start collapsing COPs again at the next Pixel Filter COP.\n    Setting the display flag on a pixel filter COP has the same effect."], "extent": [7427, 7724]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["Timing modifiers"], "extent": [7724, 7742], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Move frames to different frame numbers, modify the frame range, or\n    shift the sequence in time. Timing modifiers don\u2019t generally cook\n    image information, and so are very efficient in both memory and\n    cooking performance."], "extent": [7742, 7981]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Timing Modifiers perform a variety of editing operations and allow you\n    to cut, splice, shift and sequence frames easily."], "extent": [7981, 8115]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The following are timing modifier COPs:"], "extent": [8115, 8164]}, {"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/trim", "type": "link", "text": ["Trim"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/trim.html"}], "extent": [8164, 8192]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/extend", "type": "link", "text": ["Extend"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/extend.html"}], "extent": [8192, 8224]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/shuffle", "type": "link", "text": ["Shuffle"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/shuffle.html"}], "extent": [8224, 8258]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/warp", "type": "link", "text": ["Time Warp"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/warp.html"}], "extent": [8258, 8291]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/shift", "type": "link", "text": ["Shift"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/shift.html"}], "extent": [8291, 8321]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/reverse", "type": "link", "text": ["Reverse"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/reverse.html"}], "extent": [8321, 8355]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/timescale", "type": "link", "text": ["Time Scale"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/timescale.html"}], "extent": [8355, 8399]}], "container": true}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Most Timing Modifiers do not need to cook images, so they are very quick\n    and memory efficient. Some Timing COPs allow you to blend frames\n    together; in this case, new images are produced and this efficiency\n    advantage is lost."], "extent": [8399, 8645]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Timing modifier node tiles have a ", {"type": "em", "text": ["beige background"]}, " when they are\n    passing through data without cooking."], "extent": [8645, 8763]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Timing Modifiers are best viewed in the ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/ref/views/imgview#ref_imgview_timeline", "type": "link", "text": ["Timeline view\n    mode"], "fullpath": "/ref/views/imgview.html#ref_imgview_timeline", "fragment": "#ref_imgview_timeline"}, " . Most timing COPs have\n    handles in the timeline view."], "extent": [8763, 8935]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["Compositing/blending operators"], "extent": [8935, 8967], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Take two image inputs and composite or blend them together in\n    different ways. All compositing operators can be masked."], "extent": [8967, 9099]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Compositing operators are the heart of the compositor. They take two or\n    more image inputs and combine them in different ways in the output."], "extent": [9099, 9252]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Compositing operators have parameters that let you choose the behavior\n    of the operator in cases where the inputs have different frame ranges,\n    resolution, and/or planes. You can transform the foreground elements as\n    part of the operation, and apply ", {"scheme": null, "value": "blur_sharpen", "type": "link", "text": ["motion blur"], "fullpath": "/composite/blur_sharpen.html"}, " to animated\n    transforms."], "extent": [9252, 9575]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["See ", {"scheme": null, "value": "layers", "type": "link", "text": ["how to blend and layer images"], "fullpath": "/composite/layers.html"}, " ."], "extent": [9575, 9625]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["All compositing operations can be masked using the\n    ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/nodes/cop2/", "type": "link", "text": ["mask input"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/index.html"}, "."], "extent": [9625, 9716]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["Plane operators"], "extent": [9716, 9733], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Create, swap, or merge ", {"scheme": null, "value": "comp_terms#comp_datatypes", "type": "link", "text": ["planes"], "fullpath": "/composite/comp_terms.html#comp_datatypes", "fragment": "#comp_datatypes"}, "."], "extent": [9733, 9801]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["You will sometimes need to swap or create new\n    ", {"scheme": null, "value": "comp_terms#comp_datatypes", "type": "link", "text": ["planes"], "fullpath": "/composite/comp_terms.html#comp_datatypes", "fragment": "#comp_datatypes"}, "  to store information during\n    compositing."], "extent": [9801, 9941]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["See ", {"scheme": null, "value": "planes", "type": "link", "text": ["working with planes"], "fullpath": "/composite/planes.html"}, "."], "extent": [9941, 9984]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": ["VEX operations"], "extent": [9984, 10000], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Some COPs are ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/vex/", "type": "link", "text": ["implemented in VEX"], "fullpath": "/vex/index.html"}, " ."], "extent": [10000, 10048]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["You can create custom compositing operators using the VEX\n    language or VOPs. Some of the compositing operators shipped\n    with Houdini may also be defined this way."], "extent": [10048, 10222]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["See ", {"scheme": null, "value": "comp_vops", "type": "link", "text": ["how to create a custom COP with VOPs"], "fullpath": "/composite/comp_vops.html"}, "."], "extent": [10222, 10281]}], "container": true}], "container": true}]}, {"level": 1, "id": "subtopics", "container": true, "type": "subtopics_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [10945, 10956], "body": [{"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Basics"], "extent": [10956, 10970], "body": [{"type": "subtopics_item_group", "body": [{"ext": null, "type": "subtopics_item", "indent": 0, "text": [" ", {"scheme": null, "value": "comp_terms", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/composite/comp_terms.html"}], "role": "item", "extent": [10970, 10987]}, {"ext": null, "type": "subtopics_item", "indent": 0, "text": [" ",